===Etymology===
{{bor+|en|non|Svalbarð|g=n}} probably through Norwegian. From {{compound|non|svalr|barð|t1=cool|t2=edge, brim}}, thus roughly meaning {{mention-gloss|cold shore}}, probably alluding to the treeless landscape mostly covered with grass. The name was first attested in ''Skálholtsannáll'' from 1350, but it’s uncertain whether it referred to the modern archipelago, the more southern island [[Jan Mayen]] or a part of [[Greenland]]. Cognate with {{cog|fo|Svalbarð}}, {{cog|is|Svalbarði}} and {{cog|no|-}} {{m|nn|Svalbard}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈsvɑːlbɑː(ɹ)/|qual2=anglicized|/ˈsvɑːlbɑː(ɹ)d/}}
